WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.997 --> 00:00:16.345
The princess closed her bedroom curtains.

2
00:00:17.105 --> 00:00:19.506
She couldn't bear to look at the lake anymore.

3
00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:22.949
All that was left was mud and rocks.

4
00:00:24.129 --> 00:00:28.412
In the brown muck, eels crawled around and fishes flopped.

5
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.462
At first Ellen's parents thought she might cry.

6
00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:37.667
But no tears flowed.

7
00:00:38.527 --> 00:00:40.989
Instead the princess locked herself away.

8
00:00:44.292 --> 00:00:47.995
Under the witch's spell, she forgot about the prince.

9
00:00:55.741 --> 00:00:58.564
She forgot about everyone, even her parents.

10
00:01:00.588 --> 00:01:03.930
The palace no longer rang with the sound of her laughter.

11
00:01:09.032 --> 00:01:11.673
For a while the prince kept going to the lake.

12
00:01:15.314 --> 00:01:17.255
Finally he realized something.

13
00:01:17.275 --> 00:01:21.957
"Ellen is never coming back," he thought.

14
00:01:21.977 --> 00:01:24.358
"I must find out if she's okay."

15
00:01:25.959 --> 00:01:27.660
The prince dressed like a servant.

16
00:01:30.312 --> 00:01:33.134
Then he went to the palace, pretending to work there.

17
00:01:35.675 --> 00:01:39.778
While he shined boots, he asked other servants about Ellen.

18
00:01:40.378 --> 00:01:44.080
They all said the same thing: "The princess is dying."

19
00:01:45.281 --> 00:01:46.441
His heart sunk.

20
00:01:47.162 --> 00:01:48.523
He had to save her.

21
00:01:48.923 --> 00:01:49.543
But how?

22
00:01:49.563 --> 00:01:53.806
"I'll go away to think of a plan," he decided.

23
00:01:55.266 --> 00:01:57.588
The king and queen didn't know what to do either.

24
00:01:58.672 --> 00:02:01.094
As usual, the king was growing impatient.

25
00:02:01.114 --> 00:02:05.217
"Let's send for Kopp and Humm," the queen said.

26
00:02:05.237 --> 00:02:08.760
"Perhaps they can explain why the lake went dry.

27
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.361
Then we can fix it."

28
00:02:16.285 --> 00:02:18.086
Kopp and Humm studied the lake bed.

29
00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.762
They discussed the dry rivers and fountains and babies' tears.

30
00:02:31.643 --> 00:02:41.789
But they couldn't figure out the cause of the One afternoon a boy came to see the queen

31
00:02:41.829 --> 00:02:42.269
and king.

32
00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:45.071
He was carrying a golden plate.

33
00:02:45.091 --> 00:02:50.894
"I found this in the muddy lake bed, Your Majesties.

34
00:02:52.315 --> 00:02:54.376
I think it has a clue about the lake."

35
00:02:55.516 --> 00:02:57.958
"What?" The king took the plate.

36
00:02:58.939 --> 00:03:00.641
It was covered with writing.

37
00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.665
"There's a long poem," he said.

38
00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:11.270
"It tells of a magical way to fill the lake!"

39
00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.233
"How?" the queen cried.

40
00:03:14.253 --> 00:03:18.497
"There's a hole in the lake bed," the king explained.

41
00:03:18.517 --> 00:03:22.000
"A human must climb into that hole to plug it up."

42
00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:25.366
"Like a cork?"

43
00:03:25.726 --> 00:03:26.647
the queen asked.

44
00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:29.190
"Yes!" the king said.

45
00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:34.176
"This cork er, person must give his life."

46
00:03:35.578 --> 00:03:37.159
He looked at his wife sadly.

47
00:03:37.179 --> 00:03:40.704
"Where will we find a brave hero like that?"
